web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:5d321365204596c12a5537be999da0afdd9518a65eb9350a92ce2ed5a5f2130a","file":"preprints/Critical-mixing-in-the-Sherrington-Kirkpatrick-model-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":86,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"5b045efa957b1b3646c30a90bc69756ccb26fdf7cbd879bb4733415c35eaf4e6","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Critical-mixing-in-the-Sherrington-Kirkpatrick-model-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:5d321365204596c12a5537be999da0afdd9518a65eb9350a92ce2ed5a5f2130a","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Critical-mixing-in-the-Sherrington-Kirkpatrick-model-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L86"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:accepted-critical}\nFor every deterministic sequence $t_n\\ge0$ with $t_n=o(n^{2/3})$,\n\\[\n \\mu_J\\!\\left\\{x:\n \\norm{e^{t_n\\mathcal L_J}(x,\\cdot)-\\mu_J}_{\\TV}>\\frac14\\right\\}\n \\longrightarrow1\n\\]\nin probability over disorder. For every deterministic nonnegative integer\nsequence $k_n=o(n^{5/3})$, the same assertion holds with $P_J^{k_n}$.\nLet $\\Sigma_J=\\Cov_{\\mu_J}(X)$ and\n\\[\n R_{\\mathrm{lin},J}=\\sup_{a\\in\\R^n\\setminus\\{0\\}}\n       \\frac{\\Var_{\\mu_J}(a^{\\mathsf T}X)}{\\D_J(a^{\\mathsf T}X)}.\n\\]\nFor every positive deterministic $M_n\\to\\infty$, with probability\ntending to one both $\\norm{\\Sigma_J}$ and $R_{\\mathrm{lin},J}$ belong to\n$[n^{2/3}/M_n,M_n n^{2/3}]$."}
